cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "FAERS disproportionality analysis of fluoroquinolone-associated peripheral neuropathy (replication and extension)"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GregRR/fq-neuropathy-faers-signal"
authors:
  - family-names: Roe
    given-names: "Greg R."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3901-4568"
abstract: >-
  Independent replication of a published BCPNN disproportionality analysis of
  fluoroquinolone-associated peripheral neuropathy using public FDA Adverse Event
  Reporting System (FAERS) quarterly extracts, extended to quarters the original
  study did not cover. FAERS is spontaneous-report data; results describe reporting
  patterns, not incidence or causation.
keywords:
  - pharmacovigilance
  - FAERS
  - fluoroquinolones
  - peripheral neuropathy
  - disproportionality analysis
  - BCPNN
